WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:28.836
Tom listened to Cat's idea.

2
00:00:28.836 --> 00:00:37.053
Then he went into the Dining Hall.

3
00:00:37.053 --> 00:00:41.078
"Where's our food?" the king cried.

4
00:00:41.078 --> 00:00:44.175
"You have eaten it all," Tom said.

5
00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:46.865
"What?" the king shouted.

6
00:00:46.865 --> 00:00:49.808
Tom gulped.

7
00:00:49.808 --> 00:00:56.529
"More food!" the guests yelled.

8
00:00:56.529 --> 00:00:59.617
"I have an idea," Tom began.

9
00:00:59.617 --> 00:01:03.122
"Cat is the best mouse hunter in the kingdom.

10
00:01:03.122 --> 00:01:06.171
So Cook can bake a mouse pie."

11
00:01:06.171 --> 00:01:12.701
"A mouse pie?" the king said.

12
00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:17.621
The Dining Hall got very quiet.

13
00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:22.243
"I'm not hungry," the king said in a small voice.

14
00:01:22.243 --> 00:01:25.777
"Me neither," some lords mumbled.

15
00:01:25.777 --> 00:01:30.016
The queen hurried into the Dining Hall.

16
00:01:30.016 --> 00:01:33.747
"Did I miss the feast?" she asked.

17
00:01:33.747 --> 00:01:37.878
"I have been reading a wonderful book about food!"

18
00:01:37.878 --> 00:01:41.182
She waved a book in the air.

19
00:01:41.182 --> 00:01:45.838
Cook gasped. "My cookbook!"

20
00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:49.132
"Is it yours?" the queen asked.

21
00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:57.841
"I found it in the hallway."

22
00:01:57.841 --> 00:02:01.090
Cook did a curtsy.

23
00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.961
"Thank you, Your Majesty!

24
00:02:03.961 --> 00:02:07.161
I can make a new feast tomorrow.

25
00:02:07.161 --> 00:02:09.987
It will be delicious!"

26
00:02:09.987 --> 00:02:15.766
"A new feast?" The king groaned.

27
00:02:15.766 --> 00:02:18.511
"I don't want another feast.

28
00:02:18.511 --> 00:02:26.356
I want a nap!"

29
00:02:26.356 --> 00:02:37.321
The next day Cook made a feast just for Tom.

30
00:02:37.321 --> 00:02:41.495
"Mmm. Delicious!" Tom said.

31
00:02:41.495 --> 00:02:47.352
"Thank you, Cook!"

32
00:02:47.352 --> 00:02:51.144
"And here's something for Cat," Cook said.

33
00:02:51.144 --> 00:02:54.109
She set down a bowl.

34
00:02:54.109 --> 00:03:10.126
"Milk is almost as good as mouse pie!"
